# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
plato-republic-2.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 3 ways: plato-republic-2.logic.r1 has "O(enquire → test)" and "passes → O selected" and "¬passes → O rejected"; plato-republic-2.logic.r1.2 has "O(passes → selected)" and "O(¬passes → rejected)"; they differ when only "he remembers and is not deceived in the trial", "it ought to be that (if he remembers and is not deceived in the trial, then he is selected)", "it ought to be that (if we enquire who are the best guardians of their own conviction that what they think the interest of the State is to be the rule of their lives, then we watch them from their youth upwards and make them perform actions in which they are most likely to forget or to be deceived)" and "it ought to be that he is selected" are true, which the first allows; plato-republic-2.logic.r1.3 has "passes → O selected" and "¬passes → O rejected"
plato-republic-2.md:1: argue/answered: S2: answered no, which keeps plato-republic-2.logic.r1.2, to: Suppose "he remembers and is not deceived in the trial", "it ought to be that he is selected", "it ought to be that (if he remembers and is not deceived in the trial, then he is selected)", "it ought to be that (if we enquire who are the best guardians of their own conviction that what they think the interest of the State is to be the rule of their lives, then we watch them from their youth upwards and make them perform actions in which they are most likely to forget or to be deceived)" and "it ought to be that he is selected" are true and "it ought to be that he is rejected", "it ought to be that (if it is not so that he remembers and is not deceived in the trial, then he is rejected)" and "it ought to be that he is rejected" are false. Is S2, "We must watch them from their youth upwards, and make them perform actions in which they are most likely to forget or to be deceived, and he who remembers and is not deceived is to be selected, and he who fails in the trial is to be rejected.", true then?
plato-republic-2.logic.r1: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 2 ways: plato-republic-2.logic.r1 has nothing from it; plato-republic-2.logic.r1.2 and plato-republic-2.logic.r1.3 have "O(enquire → test)"; they differ when nothing is true, which the first allows
plato-republic-2.md:1: argue/unfaithful: plato-republic-2.logic.r1 P2 (S2): the sentence has no word of "we enquire who are the best guardians of their own conviction that what they think the interest of the State is to be the rule of their lives": is it the sentence P2 came from?
